// Official Candy Motorsport archive records. Edit this file to update historical entries.
const archive=[{"title":"Introduction","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"EST. 1985  /  JOLIET, ILLINOIS"},{"type":"text","text":"Candy Motorsport"},{"type":"heading","text":"The History of the Pink Empire"},{"type":"text","text":"Sweet on the outside. Ruthless on the inside."},{"type":"text","text":"Official career-universe heritage archive • Edition 4.6 • Weekend progress: Belgian Grand Prix FP2 (26 July 2024). Championship totals through Hungary, 21 July 2024."},{"type":"heading","text":"From Illinois to the world stage"},{"type":"text","text":"Founded by Walter Candy in 1985, Candy Motorsport grew from a workshop in Joliet into an American racing organisation with championships across stock cars, trucks and endurance racing. In 2024, the family entered Formula One under Caroline Elizabeth Candy."},{"type":"text","text":"On 7 April, Pierre Gasly brought home its first Grand Prix podium at Suzuka. On 5 May, Daniel Ricciardo secured its maiden Formula One victory from pole at Miami. At Imola on 19 May, the team reached third in the constructors’ championship after Ricciardo’s second consecutive pole and third consecutive podium."},{"type":"text","text":"On 25 May at Monaco, Ricciardo claimed his third consecutive pole and Gasly qualified second, securing the team’s first Formula One front-row lockout. The following day, Ricciardo and Gasly converted the lockout into Candy Motorsport’s first Formula One one-two finish, winning 43 points at Monaco. On 8 June in Canada, Ricciardo secured his fourth consecutive pole, with Gasly fifth. On 9 June, Gasly finished second in Canada, extending the team’s podium streak to six consecutive weekends; Ricciardo retired. On 23 June at Barcelona, Ricciardo won from fifth on the grid and Gasly finished third, securing the team’s third Formula One victory and second double podium. On 30 June at Spielberg, Gasly won from eighth on the grid, claiming his first Candy Motorsport victory and the team’s fourth F1 win. Candy closed to within 14 points of the constructors’ lead."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Pre-F1 legacy (through 2023)","Formula One (through Hungary race)"],["18 titles (recorded aggregate)","13 Grands Prix"],["247 victories","12 podiums"],["5 Cup championships","4 wins • 5 poles"],["3 Daytona 500 victories","308 constructors’ points • P3"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Archive contents"},{"type":"text","text":"01  Origins and family leadership\n02  American racing and endurance heritage\n03  Championship and victory records\n04  The Formula One project\n05  Inaugural season and Suzuka milestone\n06  Living Formula One record and update ledger\n07  Affiliate driver outing register\n08  Chinese Grand Prix weekend record\n09  Special livery design and deployment register\n10  Miami Grand Prix, first pole and first victory\n11  Emilia-Romagna Grand Prix, second pole and fourth podium\n12  Monaco Grand Prix, first one-two finish\n13  Canadian Grand Prix, fourth consecutive pole\n14  Spanish Grand Prix, third victory\n15  Austrian Grand Prix weekend record\n16  Operation Honey Badger | Ricciardo renewal\n17  Driver line-up confirmed through 2026\n18  Riccardo Adami renewal and 2025 engineering continuity\n19  British Grand Prix, pole and championship lead\n20  Hungarian Grand Prix, FP1–FP3 practice record\n21  Belgian Grand Prix weekend record (FP1–FP2 logged; FP3, qualifying and race pending)"},{"type":"text","text":"Archive scope: fictional team history and F1 Manager 2024 career results. Real-world people and brands appear within the fictional career universe. Unconfirmed details are left open rather than invented."}]},{"title":"01  Origins and family leadership","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"1985–1999 | Walter Candy and the foundations"},{"type":"text","text":"Walter Candy established the organisation in a workshop in Joliet, Illinois, in 1985. Regional racing formed the foundation of its competitive identity. Frank Maddox won regional titles in 1988 and 1990, before Jack Hollister secured Busch titles in 1994 and 1999. Russell Boone added a truck title in 1997."},{"type":"heading","text":"2000–2022 | The Candy brothers"},{"type":"text","text":"Richard Candy and Michael Candy jointly led the organisation from 2000 through 2022. Their era elevated the team into a major American racing force, with five Cup championships, three Daytona 500 triumphs and an expansion into international endurance competition."},{"type":"heading","text":"2023 onward | A new generation"},{"type":"text","text":"Caroline Elizabeth Candy assumed team leadership in 2023 before becoming Formula One team principal for the 2024 debut. Her aunt Victoria “Vicky” Candy, aged 54 at the launch, chairs the wider organisation and serves as CEO. Joliet remains the corporate headquarters; the Formula One base is outside Welwyn Garden City, Hertfordshire, England."},{"type":"heading","text":"Caroline Elizabeth Candy"},{"type":"text","text":"Born 14 February 1998. Studied mechanical engineering; performance analyst in 2020, head of race strategy in 2021 and deputy NASCAR team principal in 2022. At 26, she is intended to be the youngest Formula One team principal in this fictional timeline. Her ambition is to build a championship-winning F1 division and ultimately bring a female driver into a full-time race seat."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Leader","Role / era"],["Walter Candy","Founder, 1985"],["Richard & Michael Candy","Joint leadership, 2000–2022"],["Victoria Candy","Group chair and CEO"],["Caroline Candy","F1 team principal, 2024 onward"]]}]},{"title":"02  Racing heritage","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"The stock car dynasty"},{"type":"text","text":"Candy Motorsport’s Cup championship era was defined by Cole Mercer, Travis Kane and Dylan Cross. Mercer won the 2005 and 2007 titles; Kane followed in 2012; Cross claimed championships in 2016 and 2021. Cross remains a leading NASCAR figure in the team’s history and worked with Caroline during her rise through the organisation."},{"type":"text","text":"The programme won the Daytona 500 in 2006, 2013 and 2021. Austin Reeve’s 2023 Xfinity championship marked the final pre-F1 season with another major title."},{"type":"heading","text":"Beyond America"},{"type":"text","text":"The endurance programme expanded the team’s identity beyond stock car racing. Its record includes the 2012 GRAND-AM GT title, the 2017 IMSA GTLM title, victory in the LMP2 class at Le Mans in 2018 and the 2019 European Le Mans Series LMP2 championship."},{"type":"heading","text":"Victory distribution through 2023"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Discipline","Wins"],["Cup","89"],["Second-tier stock cars","57"],["Trucks","41"],["Endurance","36"],["Regional racing","24"],["Total","247"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Drivers in the heritage record"},{"type":"text","text":"Frank Maddox, Jack Hollister, Russell Boone, Cole Mercer, Travis Kane, Mason Briggs, Émile Beaumont, Dylan Cross and Austin Reeve. Shaw, Varga and Hart also appear in the endurance title records; full names are not yet established."}]},{"title":"03  Championship honour roll","blocks":[{"type":"table","rows":[["Year","Championship","Driver(s)"],["1988","Regional","Frank Maddox"],["1990","Regional","Frank Maddox"],["1994","Busch","Jack Hollister"],["1997","Truck","Russell Boone"],["1999","Busch","Jack Hollister"],["2001","Truck","Russell Boone"],["2005","Cup","Cole Mercer"],["2007","Cup","Cole Mercer"],["2009","Nationwide","Travis Kane"],["2012","Cup","Travis Kane"],["2012","Truck","Mason Briggs"],["2012","GRAND-AM GT","Shaw / Beaumont"],["2014","Nationwide","Dylan Cross"],["2016","Cup","Dylan Cross"],["2017","IMSA GTLM","Shaw / Beaumont"],["2019","ELMS LMP2","Beaumont / Varga / Hart"],["2021","Cup","Dylan Cross"],["2023","Xfinity","Austin Reeve"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Major race victories"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Year","Event"],["2006","Daytona 500"],["2013","Daytona 500"],["2018","24 Hours of Le Mans, LMP2 class"],["2021","Daytona 500"]]},{"type":"text","text":"The 18 championships above reconcile with the recorded aggregate. Individual race results within the 247-win total and winning drivers for the four major victories have not been established."}]},{"title":"04  The Formula One project","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Candy Motorsport entered F1 in 2024 as an American constructor with the abbreviation CND, Ferrari power and an electric-pink identity. Operation Sugar Rush is its strategic initiative to reach the front of the grid. The board’s inaugural objective is third or better in the constructors’ championship; the long-term target is the 2026 constructors’ title."},{"type":"heading","text":"Founding organisation"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Position","Appointment"],["Team principal","Caroline Candy"],["Car 1 / Car 2","Pierre Gasly / Daniel Ricciardo"],["Technical chief","Pierre Waché"],["Head of aerodynamics","Peter Prodromou"],["Sporting director","Ron Meadows"],["Founding race engineers","Riccardo Adami / William Joseph"],["Power unit","Ferrari"],["Chassis","CM-01"]]},{"type":"text","text":"At Suzuka, the race engineers were reassigned: William Joseph to Gasly and Riccardo Adami to Ricciardo. In early June 2024, Marcus Dudley accepted an offer to replace Joseph as Gasly’s race engineer under Operation Sweet Connection. Adami remains assigned to Ricciardo."},{"type":"heading","text":"Operation Sweet Connection | Marcus Dudley"},{"type":"text","text":"Recruited from Mercedes on a three-season contract expiring 31 December 2027. Annual salary: $1,430,000; signing bonus: $140,000; confirmed recruitment payment: $873,296. Whether the payment includes the signing bonus is unconfirmed. The exact acceptance date and initial driver affinity are not yet recorded."},{"type":"heading","text":"Identity and commercial portfolio"},{"type":"text","text":"The standard CM-01 livery features white bodywork, sweeping electric-pink graphics, a pink front wing, white rear wing and dark lower bodywork. Its proposed name, Sugar Rush, awaits approval. Special American liveries: Miami Sugar Vice (pink, turquoise, white); Austin American Sugar (pink, blue, white); Las Vegas Sugar Jackpot (pink, gold, black)."},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed fictional partners: Visa (title), Caterpillar, Motorola, Gatorade and FedEx. Four further sponsors were selected but their identities remain unrecorded. Total potential commercial value: $80 million."},{"type":"text","text":"Career configuration: Your Story; $40 million starting balance; facilities 5/5; car performance 4/5. Sprint races are disabled for every season."},{"type":"heading","text":"Driver academy | 10 April 2024"},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed affiliates: Jean-Philippe Moulin (68), Corinne Morel (59) and Abbi Pulling (59). Ratings are a snapshot as of 10 April 2024. Moulin has improved from 66 to 68. Pulling joined from Alpine on a five-season affiliate contract. The academy supports Caroline’s ambition to develop a female full-time F1 driver."}]},{"title":"05  2024 | The inaugural season","blocks":[{"type":"table","rows":[["Round / event","Gasly","Ricciardo","Team points"],["1 Bahrain","P9","DNF","2"],["2 Saudi Arabia","P14","P11","0"],["3 Australia","P8","P4","16"],["4 Japan","P3","P7","21"],["5 China","P10","P2","19"],["6 Miami","P4","P1","37"],["7 Imola","P4","P2","30"],["8 Monaco","P2","P1","43"],["9 Canada","P2","DNF","18"],["10 Spain","P3","P1","40"],["11 Austria","P1","P4","37"],["12 Great Britain","P3","P2","33"],["13 Hungary","P4","P12","12"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Saudi Arabia: Ricciardo finished P11 and Gasly P14; neither scored points. Bahrain retirement followed rear-wing and sidepod damage; responsibility is undetermined."},{"type":"heading","text":"7 April 2024 | First Formula One podium"},{"type":"text","text":"At Suzuka, Gasly qualified fourth and Ricciardo seventh after both reached Q3 in moderate rain. On race day Gasly finished third behind Max Verstappen and Oscar Piastri, earning 15 points. Ricciardo retained seventh and earned six points. The team collected 21 points and climbed to fourth in the constructors’ standings."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Suzuka record","Result"],["Gasly best race lap","1:30.348"],["Ricciardo best race lap","1:30.500"],["Gasly pit stop","2.554s, sixth in DHL rankings"],["Race target bonus","$1,008,332"],["Gasly championship","P7, 21 points"],["Ricciardo championship","P10, 18 points"],["Constructors’ championship","P4, 39 points"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Trophy 001: Japanese Grand Prix third place, Pierre Gasly. The first trophy of the Formula One era arrived in the team’s fourth Grand Prix."},{"type":"heading","text":"Round 13 | Hungarian Grand Prix, 19–21 July 2024"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Pierre Gasly · Car 1","Daniel Ricciardo · Car 2","Conditions"],["FP1 · Fri 19 Jul","P1 · 1:19.071","P9 · 1:19.898","Cloudy"],["FP2 · Fri 19 Jul","P9 · 1:19.053","P5 · 1:18.890","Cloudy"],["FP3 · Sat 20 Jul","P2 · 1:18.270","P3 · 1:18.518","Cloudy"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Practice was cloudy throughout. Gasly topped FP1 (1:19.071) and finished P2 in FP3 (1:18.270); Ricciardo took P5 in FP2 (1:18.890) and P3 in FP3 (1:18.518). Both reached Q3: Gasly qualified P4 (1:14.085), Ricciardo P7 (1:14.247), again in cloudy conditions. On Sunday 21 July, light rain fell during laps 7–25. Gasly finished P4 (best race lap 1:16.544), adding 12 points and earning a $504,166 race-target bonus; Ricciardo finished P12 (best race lap 1:17.939). Candy Motorsport moved to P3 in the Constructors' Championship with 308 points after 13 races."},{"type":"heading","text":"Looking ahead"},{"type":"text","text":"2025 marks the organisation’s 40th anniversary. The 2026 championship ambition remains a target, not an achieved result."}]},{"title":"06  Living Formula One records","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Season register"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Season","Starts / wins / poles / podiums","Points / position"],["2024 (ongoing)","13 / 4 / 5 / 12","308 / P3"],["Future seasons","To be recorded","To be recorded"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Grand Prix victories"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Win no.","Date / Grand Prix","Driver / grid","Notes"],["001","5 May 2024 / Miami","Daniel Ricciardo / P1","First F1 victory; home GP"],["002","26 May 2024 / Monaco","Daniel Ricciardo / P1","First team one-two finish"],["003","23 Jun 2024 / Spain","Daniel Ricciardo / P5","Second team double podium"],["004","30 Jun 2024 / Austria","Pierre Gasly / P8","First Candy victory for Gasly"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Podium and trophy register"},{"type":"table","rows":[["No.","Date / event","Driver","Result"],["001","7 Apr 2024 / Japan","Pierre Gasly","P3"],["002","21 Apr 2024 / China","Daniel Ricciardo","P2"],["003","5 May 2024 / Miami","Daniel Ricciardo","P1"],["004","19 May 2024 / Imola","Daniel Ricciardo","P2"],["005","26 May 2024 / Monaco","Daniel Ricciardo","P1"],["006","26 May 2024 / Monaco","Pierre Gasly","P2"],["007","9 Jun 2024 / Canada","Pierre Gasly","P2"],["008","23 Jun 2024 / Spain","Daniel Ricciardo","P1"],["009","23 Jun 2024 / Spain","Pierre Gasly","P3"],["010","30 Jun 2024 / Austria","Pierre Gasly","P1"],["011","7 Jul 2024 / Great Britain","Daniel Ricciardo","P2"],["012","7 Jul 2024 / Great Britain","Pierre Gasly","P3"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Pole positions and championships"},{"type":"text","text":"First F1 pole position: Daniel Ricciardo, Miami Grand Prix, 4 May 2024, 1:38.085 in moderate rain. Second pole: Ricciardo, Emilia-Romagna Grand Prix, 18 May 2024, 1:20.385 in heavy rain. No F1 drivers’ or constructors’ championships recorded at the archive cut-off. Third pole: Ricciardo, Monaco Grand Prix, 25 May 2024, 1:09.327 in partly cloudy conditions; Gasly P2, 1:09.375, first team front-row lockout. Fourth pole: Ricciardo, Canadian Grand Prix, 8 June 2024, 1:09.969; Gasly P5, 1:10.692. Fifth pole: Ricciardo, British Grand Prix, 6 July 2024, 1:26.049 in cloudy conditions; Gasly qualified P3 with a 1:26.136."},{"type":"heading","text":"Milestone register"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Date","Milestone"],["1985","Organisation founded"],["2024, Bahrain","F1 debut and first points"],["24 Mar 2024","First top-four F1 finish: Ricciardo, Australia"],["7 Apr 2024","First F1 podium: Gasly, Japan"],["21 Apr 2024","First F1 second place: Ricciardo, China"],["Pre-Miami 2024","Miami Sugar Vice activated for first home Grand Prix"],["4 May 2024","First F1 pole position: Daniel Ricciardo, Miami"],["5 May 2024","First F1 victory: Daniel Ricciardo, Miami"],["17 May 2024","First female F1 practice driver for Candy: Abbi Pulling, Imola FP1"],["18 May 2024","Second consecutive F1 pole: Daniel Ricciardo at Imola"],["19 May 2024","Fourth F1 podium; first recorded constructors’ P3 (125 points)"],["25 May 2024","Third consecutive pole (Ricciardo); first F1 front-row lockout (Gasly P2), Monaco"],["26 May 2024","First F1 one-two and double podium; Ricciardo wins Monaco, Gasly P2; 168 constructors’ points"],["Early June 2024","Marcus Dudley accepts Car 1 race engineer contract through 31 December 2027; Operation Sweet Connection recruitment milestone."],["7 June 2024","Corinne Morel makes her FP1 debut in moderate rain in Canada; all three affiliates have now appeared. Marcus Dudley’s first recorded Candy practice session."],["8 June 2024","Ricciardo takes fourth consecutive F1 pole in Canada; Gasly qualifies fifth."],["9 June 2024","Gasly finishes second in Canada, extending the team’s podium streak to six weekends. Ricciardo retires."],["22 June 2024","Gasly qualifies second in Spain, equalling his Monaco result; Ricciardo qualifies fifth, ending his four-race pole streak."],["23 June 2024","Ricciardo wins in Spain from P5; Gasly finishes P3. Third F1 victory, second double podium, seventh consecutive podium weekend; 226 points."],["30 June 2024","Gasly wins from P8 in Austria; Ricciardo P4. Fourth F1 win, tenth individual podium, eighth consecutive podium weekend; 263 points."],["Post-Austria / pre-Silverstone 2024","Operation Honey Badger: Daniel Ricciardo accepts extension through 2026."],["Pre-Silverstone 2024","Pierre Gasly confirmed to remain through 2026; no new renewal. Both race drivers secured through 2026."],["Pre-Silverstone 2024","Riccardo Adami accepts one-season extension as Car 2 race engineer through 2025."],["Pre-Silverstone 2024","British Sherbet Lemon Edition deployment confirmed."],["7 July 2024","Silverstone double podium: Ricciardo P2 and Gasly P3. Twelfth F1 podium, ninth consecutive podium weekend, and first Constructors' Championship lead with 296 points, one ahead of Red Bull."],["21 July 2024","Hungary: Gasly finishes fourth and earns 12 points plus $504,166 target bonus; Ricciardo P12. Candy Motorsport falls to P3 in Constructors' Championship with 308 points, three behind Ferrari and 22 behind Red Bull."]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Revision ledger"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Edition","In-game cut-off","Changes"],["1.0","7 Apr 2024","Founding history, honour roll and first F1 podium"],["1.1","7 Apr 2024","Saudi Arabian GP results confirmed"],["1.2","10 Apr 2024","Confirmed three affiliate drivers and ratings"],["1.3","19 Apr 2024","Affiliate outing register; Shanghai FP1"],["1.4","21 Apr 2024","Chinese GP results, second podium and weekend record"],["1.5","Pre-Miami 2024","Special livery register and Miami deployment photograph"],["1.6","Pre-Miami 2024","Livery heritage and cultural inspiration"],["1.7","4 May 2024","Miami practice and qualifying; first F1 pole position"],["1.8","5 May 2024","Miami victory, race results and confirmed standings"],["1.9","17 May 2024","Abbi Pulling FP1 debut at Imola; affiliate and milestone registers"],["2.0","19 May 2024","Imola qualifying and race; season totals, pole, podium and milestone registers"],["2.1","25 May 2024","Monaco practice and qualifying; third pole and first front-row lockout"],["2.2","26 May 2024","Monaco race victory and one-two; updated season totals, standings and honours"],["2.3","June 2024, pre-Canada","Dudley appointment and confirmed contract terms; earlier race records retained."],["2.4","7 June 2024 / Canada FP1","Morel debut, Canadian FP1 results and affiliate totals; prior records retained."],["2.5","8 June 2024 / Canada Q3","Canadian FP2–Q3 results, fourth consecutive pole, powertrain rotation and updated pole totals."],["2.6","9 June 2024 / Canada race","Canadian race results, trophy 007, updated championship and heritage totals."],["2.7","22 June 2024 / Spain qualifying","Spanish practice and qualifying records; race pending."],["2.8","23 June 2024 / Spain race","Spanish race results, victories, trophies, points, milestones and proposed race strategies."],["2.9","29 June 2024 / Austria FP3","Austrian practice results, conditions and teammate gaps."],["3.0","29 June 2024 / Austria qualifying","Austrian Q1–Q3 results, identical Q2 times and final grid positions."],["3.1","30 June 2024 / Austria race","Austrian race results, Gasly’s first Candy victory, standings, pit stop ranking, bonuses and updated season registers."],["3.2","Pre-Silverstone 2024","Ricciardo renewal confirmed; contract milestone and announcement artwork added."],["3.3","Pre-Silverstone 2024","Gasly retention announcement and artwork; existing contract distinguished from Ricciardo renewal."],["3.4","Pre-Silverstone 2024","Joint Gasly–Ricciardo 2026 driver line-up announcement artwork added to section 17."],["3.5","Pre-Silverstone 2024","Adami renewal, corrected announcement artwork and 2025 race engineering continuity added."],["3.6","Pre-Silverstone 2024","Sherbet Lemon Edition confirmed; livery register and in-game photograph added."],["3.7","7 July 2024 / British Grand Prix","Silverstone double podium, fifth pole, 12 podiums, first Constructors' Championship lead, and updated season and milestone registers."],["3.8","20 July 2024 / Hungarian GP FP3","Hungarian FP1–FP3 practice record, weather and driver comparisons; race and qualifying pending. No change to post-Silverstone championship standings."],["3.9","20 July 2024 / Hungarian Grand Prix","Relocated Hungarian FP1–FP3 report under 2024 Grand Prix Reports, renamed Round 13, added pending Qualifying and Race sections without inventing results."],["4.0","20 July 2024 / Hungarian Grand Prix Q1","Gasly P4, 1:13.991; Ricciardo P5, 1:14.058; cloudy; estimated Q1 cut-off 1:14.543. Q2, Q3 and race pending."],["4.1","20 July 2024 / Hungarian Grand Prix Q2","Gasly P3, 1:13.862; Ricciardo P5, 1:14.049; cloudy; estimated pole benchmark 1:13.745. Both advanced to Q3, race pending."],["4.2","20 July 2024 / Hungarian Grand Prix qualifying","Q3 final positions: Gasly P4, 1:14.085; Ricciardo P7, 1:14.247; cloudy. Race grid updated; Grand Prix result remains pending."],["4.3","21 July 2024 / Hungarian GP race","Full Hungarian classification, light rain laps 7–25, Gasly P4 and $504,166 target bonus, Ricciardo P12; 2024 race and all championship totals updated."],["4.4","26 July 2024 / Belgian GP FP1","Created Round 14 Belgian Grand Prix report; Gasly P5, 1:47.888 and Ricciardo P6, 1:47.975 in clear skies. FP2, FP3, qualifying and race pending; standings unchanged."],["4.5","26 July 2024 / Belgian GP FP2 (originally mislabelled)","FP2 results were initially mistaken for qualifying Q2. The attribution is superseded by the edition 4.6 correction; no Belgian qualifying result is confirmed."],["4.6","26 July 2024 / Belgian GP FP2 correction","Corrected Round 14 FP2: Gasly P2, 1:46.044; Ricciardo P10, 1:47.088 in clear skies. FP3, qualifying Q1–Q3 and race remain pending. Championship totals unchanged."]]},{"type":"text","text":"Update protocol: retain earlier history; append confirmed victories, poles, podiums and titles; update season totals and the cut-off date; record the revision. Distinguish provisional plans from achieved results. *China cumulative points are calculated from Japan totals and standard finishing points; fastest-lap bonus unconfirmed. Miami confirms cumulative points of 61 (Ricciardo), 34 (Gasly) and 95 (team), consistent with prior calculated totals plus standard finishing points. Record special livery deployments and subsequent returns to the standard design."}]},{"title":"07  Affiliate driver outing register","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed Formula One practice appearances only. Update after each affiliate outing; unreported sessions are not counted."},{"type":"heading","text":"2024 | Session log"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Date / event","Driver","Session / car","Position","Best lap"],["19 Apr / China","Jean-Philippe Moulin","FP1 / Car 1","P9","1:38.642"],["17 May / Imola","Abbi Pulling","FP1 / Car 1","P11","1:18.803"],["7 June / Canada","Corinne Morel","FP1 / Car 1","P21","1:19.446"],["5 Jul / Silverstone","Abbi Pulling","FP1 / Car 1","P9","1:32.585"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Shanghai benchmark: Daniel Ricciardo finished P4 (1:37.742), 0.900s ahead of Moulin. Fuel loads and tyre compounds are unconfirmed."},{"type":"text","text":"Imola debut: Abbi Pulling became the first female driver to represent Candy Motorsport in an official F1 practice session. She replaced Pierre Gasly in Car 1 and finished P11 (1:18.803); Daniel Ricciardo finished P2 (1:17.921), a gap of 0.882s. Fuel loads and tyre compounds are unconfirmed."},{"type":"text","text":"Montréal debut: Corinne Morel replaced Pierre Gasly in Car 1, finishing P21 (1:19.446) in moderate rain. Daniel Ricciardo finished P4 (1:17.960), 1.486s ahead (1.91%). Morel became the second female driver to represent Candy in FP1. All three affiliates have now appeared. Fuel loads and tyre compounds remain unconfirmed."},{"type":"text","text":"Silverstone FP1: Abbi Pulling replaced Pierre Gasly in Car 1 and finished P9 (1:32.585) in partly cloudy conditions. Daniel Ricciardo remained in Car 2 and finished P3 (1:32.058), 0.527s ahead. Fuel loads and tyre compounds are unconfirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Career appearance totals"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Affiliate","Recorded outings","Best session result"],["Jean-Philippe Moulin","1","P9"],["Corinne Morel","1","P21"],["Abbi Pulling","2","P9"]]}]},{"title":"08  Chinese Grand Prix | 21 April 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 5 • Shanghai International Circuit • 56 laps. Ricciardo secured the team’s best F1 finish to date and its second consecutive podium."},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend session record"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Gasly","Ricciardo"],["FP1","Moulin: P9 / 1:38.642","P4 / 1:37.742"],["FP2","P1 / 1:36.183","P3 / 1:36.563"],["FP3","P3 / 1:36.462","P2 / 1:36.450"],["Q1","P1 / 1:31.236","P5 / 1:31.562"],["Q2","P2 / 1:31.107","P3 / 1:31.161"],["Q3 / grid","P4 / 1:31.443","P5 / 1:31.571"],["Race / best lap","P10 / 1:36.117","P2 / 1:35.325"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Race record"},{"type":"text","text":"Podium: Carlos Sainz (Ferrari), Daniel Ricciardo (Candy), Lewis Hamilton (Mercedes)."},{"type":"text","text":"DHL pit stop ranking: Ricciardo P8, 2.578s. Race target: P9 or better, achieved by Ricciardo; bonus $504,166."},{"type":"text","text":"Standings: Ricciardo P7, Gasly P9, Candy P4. Standard finishing points: Ricciardo 18, Gasly 1; team 19. Calculated cumulative points: 36, 22 and 58 respectively, excluding any unconfirmed fastest-lap bonus."},{"type":"text","text":"Planned strategies: Gasly medium–hard; Ricciardo hard–soft–medium. Actual stops, compounds and cause of Gasly’s position loss are unconfirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Trophy 002 | Chinese Grand Prix"},{"type":"text","text":"Second place, Daniel Ricciardo. First Candy Motorsport podium for Ricciardo."}]},{"title":"09  Special livery register","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"2024 • CM-01 • The Candy family’s special editions celebrate its American racing heritage and the communities that welcome the team, while preserving the Pink Empire’s signature colour."},{"type":"heading","text":"American Special 01 | Miami Sugar Vice"},{"type":"text","text":"Miami Grand Prix • 5 May 2024. Turquoise and white evoke South Beach and its Art Deco streets, while electric pink recalls Miami’s neon nightlife. Candy’s first Formula One home race celebrates its journey from Joliet to the world stage. Race debut: Miami, 5 May 2024; maiden F1 victory from pole."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/images/1d8d20e6569aed.jpg"},{"type":"text","text":"Miami Sugar Vice | CM-01 in its South Beach-inspired colours."},{"type":"heading","text":"British Special | Sherbet Lemon Edition"},{"type":"text","text":"Lemon yellow bodywork, electric-pink rear wing and accents, and white detailing recall British sherbet lemon sweets and celebrate the adopted home in Hertfordshire. Round 12 • 5–7 July 2024. Final in-game design confirmed ahead of Silverstone. The standard pink-and-white livery is scheduled to return after the weekend; race results and the actual return remain pending."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/images/ad295ef5ef4587.png"},{"type":"text","text":"Sherbet Lemon Edition | Confirmed in-game CM-01 design."},{"type":"heading","text":"Future special editions"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Event / design","Palette / inspiration","Status"],["Austin / American Sugar","Pink, blue and white angular stripes honour American racing heritage and the team’s Illinois roots.","Designed; debut pending"],["Las Vegas / Sugar Jackpot","Pink, gold and black evoke the illuminated casinos and extravagant glamour of the Las Vegas Strip.","Designed; debut pending"],["Silverstone / Sherbet Lemon Edition","Lemon yellow bodywork, electric-pink rear wing and accents, and white detailing recall British sherbet lemon sweets and celebrate the adopted home in Hertfordshire.","Deployment confirmed; British GP, 5–7 July 2024"]]},{"type":"text","text":"The team will return to its signature pink-and-white colours after Miami. Each special edition’s race debut will be recorded in the heritage register."}]},{"title":"10  Miami Grand Prix | 4–5 May 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 6 • First American home Grand Prix • Miami Sugar Vice. Daniel Ricciardo secured Candy Motorsport’s maiden Formula One pole position in moderate rain, in the sixth Grand Prix weekend of the team’s inaugural season."},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend session record"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Gasly","Ricciardo"],["FP1","P5 / 1:34.511","P4 / 1:34.491"],["FP2","P11 / 1:33.686","P2 / 1:32.800"],["FP3 (rain)","P3 / 1:36.300","P10 / 1:44.004"],["Q1 (rain)","P10 / 1:38.750","P7 / 1:38.466"],["Q2 (rain)","P1 / unverified","P4 / unverified"],["Q3 (rain)","P10 / 1:49.637","P1 / 1:38.085"],["Race / best lap","P4 / 1:30.914","P1 / 1:30.375"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Q2 classification is retained as reported. Supplied lap times repeat Q1 and conflict with the Q2 ordering; verification is pending. The cause of Gasly’s Q3 deficit is unconfirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Pole position 001 | Daniel Ricciardo"},{"type":"text","text":"4 May 2024. Ricciardo qualified on pole in the Ferrari-powered CM-01, carrying the Miami Sugar Vice colours. Gasly qualified tenth. The achievement adds a first pole to the team’s two podiums and marks another milestone in Operation Sugar Rush under Caroline Candy."},{"type":"text","text":"Race completed on 5 May 2024: Ricciardo won from pole and Gasly recovered from tenth to fourth. See the race record below."},{"type":"heading","text":"Trophy 003 | Maiden Formula One victory"},{"type":"text","text":"5 May 2024 • Miami • 57 laps. Daniel Ricciardo won ahead of Charles Leclerc (Ferrari) and Oscar Piastri (McLaren). Pierre Gasly gained six positions to finish fourth. Candy Motorsport scored 37 standard finishing points (25 and 12). Both drivers met their race targets, earning $1,008,332 in additional bonuses."},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed standings: Ricciardo P5 (61 points); Gasly P9 (34 points); Candy Motorsport P4 (95 points). The victory was achieved in the Miami Sugar Vice livery at the team’s first American home Grand Prix."},{"type":"text","text":"Approved pre-race plans: Ricciardo soft–medium–soft; Gasly medium–hard. Actual pit stops, race tyre usage and fastest-lap award are not confirmed."}]},{"title":"11  Emilia-Romagna Grand Prix | 17–19 May 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 7 • Imola • 63 laps. Ricciardo secured back-to-back poles and a third consecutive personal podium. Candy Motorsport advanced to third in the constructors’ standings, reaching its season position target provisionally."},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend session record"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Gasly / affiliate","Ricciardo"],["FP1","Pulling P11 / 1:18.803","P2 / 1:17.921"],["FP2","P5 / 1:17.277","P2 / 1:16.958"],["FP3 (heavy rain)","P8 / 1:25.454","P6 / 1:25.245"],["Q1 (dry)","P5 / 1:14.879","P6 / 1:15.099"],["Q2 (heavy rain)","P4 / unverified","P3 / unverified"],["Q3 (heavy rain)","P4 / 1:20.609","P1 / 1:20.385"],["Race / best lap","P4 / 1:15.701","P2 / 1:15.632"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Q2 supplied times repeat Q1 and conflict with the reported classification; positions retained, lap times unverified. Q1 estimated cut-off: 1:15.306; Q2 estimated pole: 1:14.750."},{"type":"heading","text":"Pole 002 and trophy 004"},{"type":"text","text":"18 May: Ricciardo took pole in heavy rain, 0.224s ahead of Gasly in fourth. 19 May: Max Verstappen (Red Bull) won ahead of Ricciardo (Candy) and Carlos Sainz (Ferrari). Gasly finished fourth. Ricciardo scored 18 points and Gasly 12; both race targets were met, earning $1,008,332 in bonuses."},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed standings: Ricciardo P4 (79 points); Gasly P8 (46 points); Candy Motorsport P3 (125 points). The team scored 30 points. Proposed strategies: medium to hard for both, with Gasly stopping around lap 25 and Ricciardo around lap 28. Actual stops, tyre usage and fastest-lap award are unconfirmed."}]},{"title":"12  Monaco Grand Prix | 24–26 May 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 8 • Monte Carlo • 78 laps. Candy Motorsport entered the weekend third in the constructors’ championship on 125 points, 11 ahead of McLaren. Both regular drivers participated throughout practice."},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend session record"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Gasly","Ricciardo"],["FP1","P3 / 1:15.000","P7 / 1:15.626"],["FP2","P5 / 1:14.415","P3 / 1:14.292"],["FP3","P4 / 1:14.223","P7 / 1:14.376"],["Q1","P4 / 1:09.860","P7 / 1:10.092"],["Q2","P6 / 1:09.710","P2 / 1:09.432"],["Q3","P2 / 1:09.375","P1 / 1:09.327"],["Race / best lap","P2 / 1:13.935","P1 / 1:12.935"]]},{"type":"text","text":"FP1 was clear; Q1 and Q3 were partly cloudy. Other session weather is unconfirmed. Estimated Q1 cut-off: 1:10.299; estimated pole after Q2: 1:09.213."},{"type":"heading","text":"Pole 003 | First front-row lockout"},{"type":"text","text":"25 May: Daniel Ricciardo secured his third consecutive pole, following Miami and Imola. Pierre Gasly qualified second, 0.048s behind, achieving his best Candy qualifying result to date. This was the organisation’s first Formula One front-row lockout."},{"type":"heading","text":"Trophies 005 and 006 | First Formula One one-two finish"},{"type":"text","text":"26 May 2024. Daniel Ricciardo won the Monaco Grand Prix ahead of Pierre Gasly and Max Verstappen (Red Bull). Candy Motorsport scored 43 standard finishing points (25 and 18). Both drivers met their race targets, earning $1,008,332 in additional bonuses. This is the team’s second F1 victory, first double podium and sixth individual podium."},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed standings: Ricciardo P3 (104 points); Gasly P6 (64 points); Candy Motorsport P3 (168 points). Selected pre-race strategies: Ricciardo soft–hard, target lap 30; Gasly medium–hard, target lap 36. Actual pit stops and tyre usage are unconfirmed. No fastest-lap bonus is reflected in the supplied points totals."}]},{"title":"13  Canadian Grand Prix | 7–9 June 2024","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"Round 9 • Circuit Gilles-Villeneuve • 70 laps. The team entered the weekend third in the constructors’ standings with 168 points. FP1 took place in moderate rain on 7 June."},{"type":"text","text":"Weekend session record"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Gasly / affiliate","Ricciardo"],["FP1 / moderate rain","Morel P21 / 1:19.446","P4 / 1:17.960"],["FP2 / moderate rain","P1 / 1:16.757","P5 / 1:17.286"],["FP3 / clear","P5 / 1:16.362","P6 / 1:16.386"],["Q1","P5 / 1:12.129","P8 / 1:12.354"],["Q2 / clear","P8 / 1:12.090","P2 / 1:11.876"],["Q3","P5 / 1:10.692","P1 / 1:09.969"],["Race / best lap","P2 / 1:15.503","DNF / 1:20.172"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Affiliate milestone and engineering debut"},{"type":"heading","text":"Morel completed her first recorded F1 practice outing, with Marcus Dudley assigned to Car 1 for his first recorded Candy Motorsport practice session. Ricciardo remained with Riccardo Adami. Gasly returned for FP2 and led the session in moderate rain, his first recorded session with Dudley. Both cars received fresh ERS units after FP3; engines were at 63% and gearboxes at 57% before qualifying."},{"type":"heading","text":"Pole 004 | Fourth consecutive pole"},{"type":"text","text":"8 June 2024. Ricciardo secured pole for the fourth consecutive Grand Prix, following Miami, Imola and Monaco. Gasly qualified fifth, 0.723s behind. Estimated Q1 cut-off: 1:12.614. Q1 and Q3 weather are unconfirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Trophy 007 | Canadian Grand Prix podium"},{"type":"text","text":"9 June 2024. Max Verstappen (Red Bull) won ahead of Pierre Gasly (Candy Motorsport) and Carlos Sainz (Ferrari). Gasly gained three positions from fifth on the grid, scoring 18 points and earning a $504,166 race target bonus. Ricciardo retired from the race after starting on pole; the cause and retirement lap are unconfirmed. This is the team’s seventh individual F1 podium and sixth consecutive podium weekend."},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed standings: Ricciardo P3 (104 points); Gasly P5 (82 points); Candy Motorsport P3 (186 points). Pre-race conditions: light rain, 1.46 mm track water. Proposed strategies: Ricciardo intermediate to medium, target lap 32; Gasly intermediate to soft, target lap 35. Actual stops and tyre usage are unconfirmed."}]},{"title":"14  Spanish Grand Prix | 21–23 June 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 10 • Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya • 66 laps. Both regular drivers completed practice. Candy Motorsport entered the race third in the constructors’ standings with 186 points."},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend session record"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Gasly","Ricciardo"],["FP1","P7 / 1:18.279","P3 / 1:17.936"],["FP2","P5 / 1:17.073","P7 / 1:17.319"],["FP3","P6 / 1:17.154","P2 / 1:16.838"],["Q1","P2 / 1:12.590","P7 / 1:13.038"],["Q2","P3 / 1:12.533","P5 / 1:12.620"],["Q3","P2 / 1:12.348","P5 / 1:12.614"],["Race / best lap","P3 / 1:15.015","P1 / 1:15.291"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Estimated pole time after Q2: 1:12.225. Weather and tyre usage are unconfirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Qualifying | Gasly equals career team best"},{"type":"text","text":"22 June 2024. Gasly qualified second, equalling his Monaco qualifying result. Ricciardo qualified fifth, 0.266s behind, ending his four consecutive poles. Both drivers met the internal top-five qualifying objective."},{"type":"heading","text":"Trophies 008 and 009 | Third Formula One victory"},{"type":"text","text":"23 June 2024. Daniel Ricciardo (Candy Motorsport) won ahead of Charles Leclerc (Ferrari) and Pierre Gasly (Candy Motorsport). Ricciardo gained four positions from fifth on the grid. Gasly scored 15 points and Ricciardo 25, for 40 team points. Both met their race targets, earning $1,008,332 in bonuses. This was the team’s ninth individual podium and seventh consecutive podium weekend."},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed standings: Ricciardo P3 (129 points); Gasly P5 (97 points); Candy Motorsport P3 (226 points). Selected pre-race strategies: Gasly soft–hard–medium, target stops around laps 21 and 46; Ricciardo medium–hard–soft, around laps 25 and 47. Both estimated at 1:23:02. Starting conditions partly cloudy, 0.00 mm track water, forecast rain probability 0–5%. Actual pit stops, tyre usage and fastest-lap award are unconfirmed."}]},{"title":"15  Austrian Grand Prix | 28–30 June 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 11 • Red Bull Ring • 71 laps. Both regular drivers completed practice. Candy Motorsport entered the weekend third in the constructors’ standings with 226 points. Standard non-sprint weekend."},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend session record"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Gasly","Ricciardo"],["FP1 / light rain","P2 / 1:08.121","P8 / 1:08.708"],["FP2 / light rain","P2 / 1:07.287","P8 / 1:07.781"],["FP3 / clear","P7 / 1:07.347","P2 / 1:06.875"],["Q1","P10 / 1:03.749","P5 / 1:03.441"],["Q2","P2 / 1:03.267","P3 / 1:03.267"],["Q3","P8 / 1:03.503","P4 / 1:03.279"],["Race / best lap","P1 / 1:06.366","P4 / 1:06.764"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Gasly led the team in both Friday sessions, by 0.587s in FP1 and 0.494s in FP2. Ricciardo reversed the order in clear conditions on Saturday, finishing 0.472s ahead. At least one Candy driver finished second in each practice session. Fuel loads, tyre compounds and setup satisfaction are unconfirmed."},{"type":"text","text":"Estimated pole time after Q2: 1:03.126. Both drivers recorded identical displayed Q2 times, 0.141s off the estimate. Qualifying weather and tyre usage are unconfirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Qualifying | Both cars reach Q3"},{"type":"text","text":"29 June 2024. Ricciardo qualified fourth and Gasly eighth, separated by 0.224s. Both recorded their fastest qualifying laps in Q2."},{"type":"heading","text":"Trophy 010 | Gasly’s first Candy Motorsport victory"},{"type":"text","text":"30 June 2024. Pierre Gasly (Candy Motorsport) won ahead of Carlos Sainz (Ferrari) and Charles Leclerc (Ferrari). Gasly gained seven positions from eighth on the grid and scored 25 points; Ricciardo finished fourth from fourth on the grid, scoring 12. Both met their race targets, earning $1,008,332 in bonuses. Ricciardo ranked eighth in the DHL pit stop list with a 2.516s stop. This was the fourth team victory, tenth individual podium and eighth consecutive podium weekend."},{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed standings: Ricciardo P3 (141 points); Gasly P5 (122 points); constructors: Ferrari 277, Red Bull 270, Candy Motorsport 263 (P3). Candy trails Ferrari by 14 points and Red Bull by seven. Selected pre-race strategies: Gasly D, medium–hard–intermediate (estimated 1:18:29); Ricciardo C, medium–hard–intermediate (1:18:16). Starting conditions partly cloudy, 0.00 mm track water; forecast rain probability reached 50% late in the race. Intermediate stops were conditional on actual weather. Actual pit laps, tyre usage, race weather and fastest-lap award are unconfirmed."}]},{"title":"16  Operation Honey Badger | Ricciardo renewal","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Ahead of the 2024 British Grand Prix, Daniel Ricciardo accepted a contract extension to remain with Candy Motorsport through the end of the 2026 season. The agreement secures the team’s inaugural Formula One race winner for its 40th anniversary campaign and its 2026 constructors’ championship target."},{"type":"text","text":"At the announcement: three victories, four pole positions, five individual podiums and 141 championship points (P3). The submitted annual salary was $9,000,000; final financial terms and exact acceptance date remain unverified."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/images/9bb44452d93357.jpg"},{"type":"text","text":"Fictional pre-Silverstone contract announcement artwork."}]},{"title":"17  Driver line-up confirmed through 2026","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Ahead of the 2024 British Grand Prix, Candy Motorsport confirmed that Pierre Gasly will remain with the team through 2026. This announcement reflects his existing commitment, not a newly signed contract extension. Together with Daniel Ricciardo’s accepted renewal, it secures the inaugural driver pairing through the team’s 2026 constructors’ championship target."},{"type":"text","text":"At the announcement, Gasly had one Candy Motorsport victory, five individual podiums and 122 championship points (P5), following his maiden team victory in Austria. No new financial terms or contract acceptance date are recorded for Gasly."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/images/ef9c9f83ce0319.jpg"},{"type":"text","text":"Fictional pre-Silverstone driver retention announcement artwork."},{"type":"heading","text":"2026 driver line-up | Joint announcement"},{"type":"text","text":"Pierre Gasly and Daniel Ricciardo confirmed together through 2026. The joint announcement celebrates continuity in the inaugural driver pairing; it does not represent a new Gasly contract."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/images/1f1cfe23d86609.jpg"},{"type":"text","text":"Fictional pre-Silverstone joint driver line-up announcement artwork."}]},{"title":"18  Riccardo Adami renewal | 2025 continuity","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Ahead of the British Grand Prix, Riccardo Adami accepted a one-season extension to remain Daniel Ricciardo’s Car 2 race engineer for 2025, through 31 December. The submitted offer was $1,852,000 annually with a ×0.50 breakout multiplier. Final financial terms and the precise acceptance date remain unverified."},{"type":"text","text":"Marcus Dudley remains partnered with Pierre Gasly in Car 1 through 2027. Both race-winning driver–engineer partnerships are therefore retained for the team’s 40th anniversary campaign. Operation Sweet Connection is complete."},{"type":"image","src":"assets/images/2078c5c132344e.jpg"},{"type":"text","text":"Fictional contract announcement artwork, corrected to identify Adami as Car 2 race engineer."}]},{"title":"19  British Grand Prix | Silverstone 2024","blocks":[{"type":"heading","text":"British Grand Prix | Free Practice"},{"type":"text","text":"Candy Motorsport arrived at Silverstone with its special Sherbet Lemon livery. Abbi Pulling participated in FP1, replacing Pierre Gasly in Car 1."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Driver","Position","Best lap","Conditions"],["FP1","Daniel Ricciardo","P3","1:32.058","Partly cloudy"],["FP1","Abbi Pulling","P9","1:32.585","Partly cloudy"],["FP2","Daniel Ricciardo","P1","1:30.797","Cloudy"],["FP2","Pierre Gasly","P4","1:31.089","Cloudy"],["FP3","Pierre Gasly","P4","1:31.119","Cloudy"],["FP3","Daniel Ricciardo","P5","1:31.173","Cloudy"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Ricciardo topped FP2, while both Candy Motorsport drivers finished inside the top five in FP3. Pulling completed her Silverstone FP1 academy outing in ninth place."},{"type":"heading","text":"British Grand Prix | Qualifying"},{"type":"text","text":"Daniel Ricciardo secured pole position at Silverstone, his fifth pole for Candy Motorsport. Pierre Gasly qualified third, giving the team two cars in the top three."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Driver","Position","Best lap","Conditions"],["Q1","Daniel Ricciardo","P7","1:26.798","Cloudy"],["Q1","Pierre Gasly","P4","1:26.325","Cloudy"],["Q2","Daniel Ricciardo","P2","1:26.259","Cloudy"],["Q2","Pierre Gasly","P9","1:26.325","Cloudy"],["Q3","Daniel Ricciardo","P1","1:26.049","Cloudy"],["Q3","Pierre Gasly","P3","1:26.136","Cloudy"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Ricciardo improved through qualifying to secure pole position, with Gasly just 0.087 seconds behind in Q3. The Sherbet Lemon cars will start the British Grand Prix from first and third."},{"type":"heading","text":"British Grand Prix | Race Results"},{"type":"text","text":"Candy Motorsport secured a double podium at Silverstone. Daniel Ricciardo finished second behind Max Verstappen, while Pierre Gasly finished third. The result moved Candy Motorsport into first place in the Constructors' Championship for the first time."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Position","Driver","Team","Best lap"],["P1","Max Verstappen","Red Bull","Not recorded"],["P2","Daniel Ricciardo","Candy Motorsport","1:31.116"],["P3","Pierre Gasly","Candy Motorsport","1:32.519"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Championship Standings | After Silverstone"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Constructors' Championship","Points"],["P1 Candy Motorsport","296"],["P2 Red Bull","295"],["P3 Ferrari","278"]]},{"type":"table","rows":[["Drivers' Championship","Points"],["P2 Daniel Ricciardo","159"],["P4 Pierre Gasly","137"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Race Weekend Achievements"},{"type":"text","text":"Ricciardo and Gasly scored 33 championship points combined. Both drivers achieved their race targets, earning Candy Motorsport $1,008,332 in bonuses. Gasly recorded a 2.573-second pit stop, ranked tenth in the DHL Top 10 Fastest Pit Stops."},{"type":"text","text":"The British Grand Prix marked Candy Motorsport's first lead of the Formula One Constructors' Championship, holding a one-point advantage over Red Bull after twelve rounds. The team celebrated the achievement wearing its special Silverstone Sherbet Lemon livery."}]},{"title":"20  Round 13 - Hungarian Grand Prix | 20th July 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 13 · Hungaroring, Hungary · 19–21 July 2024. Complete weekend record: Free Practice, Qualifying and Grand Prix race. Qualifying took place 20 July; the race was held 21 July."},{"type":"heading","text":"Hungarian Grand Prix | Free Practice"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Driver","Position","Best lap","Conditions"],["FP1 · 19 Jul","Pierre Gasly","P1","1:19.071","Cloudy"],["FP1 · 19 Jul","Daniel Ricciardo","P9","1:19.898","Cloudy"],["FP2 · 19 Jul","Daniel Ricciardo","P5","1:18.890","Cloudy"],["FP2 · 19 Jul","Pierre Gasly","P9","1:19.053","Cloudy"],["FP3 · 20 Jul","Pierre Gasly","P2","1:18.270","Cloudy"],["FP3 · 20 Jul","Daniel Ricciardo","P3","1:18.518","Cloudy"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Practice performance summary"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Faster Candy driver","Teammate gap"],["FP1","Pierre Gasly","0.827s"],["FP2","Daniel Ricciardo","0.163s"],["FP3","Pierre Gasly","0.248s"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Gasly led FP1, while Ricciardo moved from ninth in FP1 to fifth in FP2. Both drivers finished in the top three in FP3, Gasly second and Ricciardo third. Gasly improved from 1:19.071 in FP1 to 1:18.270 in FP3 (0.801s); Ricciardo improved from 1:19.898 to 1:18.518 (1.380s)."},{"type":"text","text":"Both race drivers took part in all three practice sessions; no affiliate-driver outing was recorded at Hungary. Tyre compounds, fuel loads and setup satisfaction were not supplied."},{"type":"heading","text":"Hungarian Grand Prix | Qualifying"},{"type":"text","text":"Qualifying completed in cloudy conditions on 20 July 2024. Q1: Gasly P4 (1:13.991), Ricciardo P5 (1:14.058), estimated cut-off 1:14.543. Q2: Gasly P3 (1:13.862), Ricciardo P5 (1:14.049), with an estimated pole benchmark of 1:13.745. Q3: Gasly qualified P4 (1:14.085), Ricciardo P7 (1:14.247), a teammate gap of 0.162s. Both Q3 laps were slower than their respective Q2 laps: Gasly by 0.223s and Ricciardo by 0.198s. Actual pole time and other drivers' Q3 results have not been supplied."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Qualifying session","Pierre Gasly","Daniel Ricciardo"],["Q1 · Cloudy","P4 · 1:13.991","P5 · 1:14.058"],["Q2 · Cloudy","P3 · 1:13.862","P5 · 1:14.049"],["Q3 · Cloudy / final grid","P4 · 1:14.085","P7 · 1:14.247"]]},{"type":"table","rows":[["Q1 session detail","Recorded value"],["Estimated cut-off time","1:14.543"],["Gasly gap below estimated cut-off","0.552s"],["Ricciardo gap below estimated cut-off","0.485s"],["Track conditions","Cloudy"]]},{"type":"table","rows":[["Q2 session detail","Recorded value"],["Estimated pole time","1:13.745"],["Gasly improvement from Q1","0.129s"],["Ricciardo improvement from Q1","0.009s"],["Gasly gap to estimated pole","0.117s"],["Ricciardo gap to estimated pole","0.304s"],["Track conditions","Cloudy"]]},{"type":"table","rows":[["Q3 session detail","Recorded value"],["Conditions","Cloudy"],["Gasly qualifying position","P4 · 1:14.085"],["Ricciardo qualifying position","P7 · 1:14.247"],["Teammate gap","0.162s"],["Gasly difference vs Q2","+0.223s"],["Ricciardo difference vs Q2","+0.198s"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Hungarian Grand Prix | Race"},{"type":"text","text":"Hungarian Grand Prix, Sunday 21 July 2024. Light rain affected laps 7–25. Gasly qualified fourth and finished fourth, setting a best race lap of 1:16.544 and scoring 12 championship points. Ricciardo started seventh and finished twelfth, with a best race lap of 1:17.939 and no points. The drivers' reported best laps are not confirmed as the overall fastest lap of the race. Gasly met his race target, securing a $504,166 team bonus; Ricciardo's target outcome was not supplied."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Driver","Starting grid","Finish","Best race lap","Championship points"],["Pierre Gasly","P4","P4","1:16.544","12"],["Daniel Ricciardo","P7","P12","1:17.939","0"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Grand Prix | Full race classification"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Finish","Driver","Constructor","Points"],["1","Max Verstappen","Red Bull","25"],["2","Charles Leclerc","Ferrari","18"],["3","Carlos Sainz","Ferrari","15"],["4","Pierre Gasly","Candy Motorsport","12"],["5","Sergio Pérez","Red Bull","10"],["6","Yuki Tsunoda","RB","8"],["7","Lance Stroll","Aston Martin","6"],["8","George Russell","Mercedes","4"],["9","Fernando Alonso","Aston Martin","2"],["10","Ayumu Iwasa","RB","1"],["11","Lewis Hamilton","Mercedes","0"],["12","Daniel Ricciardo","Candy Motorsport","0"],["13","Oscar Piastri","McLaren","0"],["14","Nico Hülkenberg","Haas","0"],["15","Zhou Guanyu","Kick Sauber","0"],["16","Kevin Magnussen","Haas","0"],["17","Valtteri Bottas","Kick Sauber","0"],["18","Esteban Ocon","Alpine","0"],["19","Lando Norris","McLaren","0"],["20","Victor Martins","Alpine","0"],["21 (DNF)","Logan Sargeant","Williams","0"],["22 (DNF)","Alexander Albon","Williams","0"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Retirements: Logan Sargeant (P21, DNF) and Alexander Albon (P22, DNF). Light rain occurred from laps 7 through 25; exact compound choices, pit stops, and the cause of each retirement are not confirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Race-day performance and commercial result"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Metric","Recorded result"],["Wet-weather period","Light rain · Laps 7–25"],["Gasly start / finish","P4 / P4"],["Ricciardo start / finish","P7 / P12"],["Gasly race target","Met"],["Gasly race-target bonus","$504,166"],["Candy Motorsport team points","12"],["Race podium","Max Verstappen P1 · Charles Leclerc P2 · Carlos Sainz P3"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Championship standings | After Hungary (Round 13)"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Pos","Constructor","Points"],["1","Red Bull","330"],["2","Ferrari","311"],["3","Candy Motorsport","308"],["4","McLaren","166"],["5","Mercedes","98"],["6","Aston Martin","56"],["7","RB","39"],["8","Kick Sauber","2"],["9","Alpine","2"],["10","Williams","1"],["11","Haas","0"]]},{"type":"table","rows":[["Pos","Driver","Constructor","Points"],["1","Max Verstappen","Red Bull","224"],["2","Carlos Sainz","Ferrari","167"],["3","Daniel Ricciardo","Candy Motorsport","159"],["4","Pierre Gasly","Candy Motorsport","149"],["5","Charles Leclerc","Ferrari","144"],["6","Sergio Pérez","Red Bull","106"],["7","Lando Norris","McLaren","86"],["8","Oscar Piastri","McLaren","80"],["9","Lewis Hamilton","Mercedes","60"],["10","George Russell","Mercedes","38"],["11","Yuki Tsunoda","RB","35"],["12","Lance Stroll","Aston Martin","31"],["13","Fernando Alonso","Aston Martin","25"],["14","Ayumu Iwasa","RB","4"],["15","Valtteri Bottas","Kick Sauber","2"],["16","Esteban Ocon","Alpine","2"],["17","Alexander Albon","Williams","1"],["18","Nico Hülkenberg","Haas","0"],["19","Kevin Magnussen","Haas","0"],["20","Zhou Guanyu","Kick Sauber","0"],["21","Logan Sargeant","Williams","0"],["22","Victor Martins","Alpine","0"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Red Bull leads the Constructors' Championship on 330 points, Ferrari follows with 311 and Candy Motorsport drops to third with 308, three points behind Ferrari and 22 behind Red Bull. Ricciardo is third in the Drivers' Championship on 159 points; Gasly fourth with 149."},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend status"},{"type":"text","text":"Round 13 complete after the Hungarian Grand Prix race on 21 July 2024. Candy Motorsport scored 12 points through Gasly's P4; Ricciardo finished P12. Constructors: P3 with 308 points. Drivers: Ricciardo P3 (159), Gasly P4 (149). Next race: Belgian Grand Prix."}]},{"title":"21  Round 14 - Belgian Grand Prix | 28th July 2024","blocks":[{"type":"text","text":"Round 14 · Circuit de Spa-Francorchamps, Belgium · 26–28 July 2024. Confirmed results: FP1 and FP2. FP3, qualifying Q1–Q3, and the Grand Prix race have not yet been supplied."},{"type":"heading","text":"Belgian Grand Prix | Free Practice"},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Driver","Position","Best lap","Conditions"],["FP1 · 26 Jul","Pierre Gasly","P5","1:47.888","Clear skies"],["FP1 · 26 Jul","Daniel Ricciardo","P6","1:47.975","Clear skies"],["FP2 · 26 Jul","Pierre Gasly","P2","1:46.044","Clear skies"],["FP2 · 26 Jul","Daniel Ricciardo","P10","1:47.088","Clear skies"],["FP3","Pierre Gasly","Pending","Pending","Pending"],["FP3","Daniel Ricciardo","Pending","Pending","Pending"]]},{"type":"text","text":"Both race drivers took part in FP1 and FP2 in clear skies. FP1: Gasly P5 (1:47.888), Ricciardo P6 (1:47.975), a 0.087s gap. FP2: Gasly P2 (1:46.044), Ricciardo P10 (1:47.088), a 1.044s gap. Relative to FP1, Gasly improved his best lap by 1.844s and Ricciardo by 0.887s. Tyre compounds, fuel loads, setup satisfaction and longer-run performance are unconfirmed."},{"type":"heading","text":"Belgian Grand Prix | Qualifying"},{"type":"text","text":"Belgian qualifying has not yet been reported. Q1, Q2, Q3 and the final starting grid remain pending."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Session","Pierre Gasly","Daniel Ricciardo"],["Q1","Pending","Pending"],["Q2","Pending","Pending"],["Q3 / Final grid","Pending","Pending"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Belgian Grand Prix | Race"},{"type":"text","text":"Awaiting race classification, weather, strategy, best race laps, scoring and championship updates. No Belgian race result has been recorded."},{"type":"table","rows":[["Driver","Starting grid","Finish","Best race lap","Points"],["Pierre Gasly","Pending","Pending","Pending","Pending"],["Daniel Ricciardo","Pending","Pending","Pending","Pending"]]},{"type":"heading","text":"Weekend status"},{"type":"text","text":"Belgian FP1 and FP2 completed; FP3, qualifying Q1–Q3 and the race are not yet confirmed in the archive. Championship standings remain as after Hungary: Candy Motorsport P3 with 308 points, Ferrari 311 and Red Bull 330."}]}];
